    "id": "C1",
    "text": "Before the fix, accessing response.elapsed on MockTransport responses raises a RuntimeError.",
    "source_quote": "Previously, accessing `response.elapsed` on MockTransport responses would raise `RuntimeError`:",
    "testable": true,
    "expect": "differs"
   },
   {
    "id": "C2",
    "text": "After the fix, MockTransport automatically sets response.elapsed to timedelta(0) for both sync and async requests.",
    "source_quote": "Fixes MockTransport to automatically set `response.elapsed` to `timedelta(0)` for both sync and async requests, eliminating boilerplate and matching real transport behavior.",
    "testable": true,
    "expect": "differs"
   },
   {
    "id": "C3",
    "text": "After the fix, accessing response.elapsed returns timedelta(0) without raising an error.",
    "source_quote": "print(response.elapsed)  # 0:00:00 \u2713",
    "testable": true,
    "expect": "differs"
   },
   {
    "id": "C4",
    "text": "After the fix, users no longer need to manually set resp.elapsed = timedelta(0) in their handler functions.",
    "source_quote": "Users had to add boilerplate in every handler:\n```python\ndef handler(request):\n    resp = httpx.Response(200, json={\"text\": \"Hello, world!\"})\n    resp.elapsed = timedelta(0)  # Boilerplate needed\n    return resp\n```",
    "testable": true,
    "expect": "differs"
   }
  ],
